 "note": "AM run. Checked 75 people and filed 17 bullets across 9 people, each verified on its source page by the parent and read back in the Sheet exactly once. Fresh sweep: none found \u2014 every in-window directory item was already filed (Evans and Goettl's Nov 14 Brown goals, Tebo's Nov 13 goal, Walczyk's re-election, Szafran's scholarship-drive item), Clarkson women's hockey had no Nov 15 game, and the Nov 15 college recaps named no directory member; all three fresh slots were left empty rather than stretched. Strongest rotation find: Daniel Paladin's church-plant transition gained its details \u2014 Alan Daniels and Paul Brown are joining the plant, Rick Sinclair takes pastoral leadership of the Potsdam congregation, and Paul Brown stays on staff through the transition. Also filed: Joye Levendusky's seventh place at the 2026 U.S. Open and her World Team Trials qualification and ninth pre-seed; Michael Jent's Spring 2021 President's List and Fall 2020 Part-Time Honors (both section-checked on the SUNY Canton honors pages); Julia Fulton's Hope College major, CAIR Coalition work, and Lighthouse Immigrant Advocates coordinator role; Jeff McGrath's SUNY Potsdam Computer Science Alumni Board of Advisors service and his 2017 presidency of Nicholville Telephone Company; two Jessica Hurlbut podcast appearances (MFI Leaders and Growing Home Together); Micah McCulley's Empire 8 indoor mile top-eight finish; Haydn Demers-St.Hilaire's Empire 8 President's List; and two David Tulloch sermons from the CFC feed. Not filed: Michelle Johnston's Shaffer Award, Joye Levendusky's Bill Farrell seeding, and Wayne Brown's Chrisman Commentary interview were all already on file in the live Sheet (the interview is the source behind Brown's on-file Gather Markets bullet), so the batch claims were discarded. One flag: the May 7, 2024 SUNY Potsdam Honors Convocation program again places Tiara Palazzo-Cross, not Mallory Greene, after the Eola Pitz Memorial Scholarship description \u2014 the same open question on Greene's record, noted here as a reminder only. 4 candidates added to Research Command. Unharvested photo leads flagged by JD: Christine Sutter, Emily Criscitello, Jale -, Joann Duclos, Joe Charlebois, Katelyn Tomford, Kayla Hettel, Max Ferran, Megan Converse."
